# TypeScript Rules

- No implicit `any`.
- Avoid unsafe type assertions.
- Use discriminated unions for state and domain models.
- Ensure exhaustive switch handling.
- Keep types separate from runtime logic.
- Strengthen generics where necessary.
- Check memorybank for previously learned type hardening lessons.
